<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3408" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκραιφνής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
		derived by Sch.<i><span class="en">
			Th.
			1.52
		</span></i>, etc., from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκεραιο-φανής,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκέραιος</span>
			, <i>unmixed pure</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόρης ἀ. αἷμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					537
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJProoem.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πενία ἀ.</span>
			<i>sheer, utter</i> poverty, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.191
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Corn.
			</span></i> Long.). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.100
				</span></i>
			; <i>honestly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				2.30
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έστατον</span> (but may be
			Adj.) <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.319
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>untouched, inviolate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				1052
			</span></i>; in 
				Att.
			 Prose only <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.19
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				52
			</span></i>; freq. later, as <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				6.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Aed.</u>
				1.10
			</span></i>, al.; <i>innocent</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.515
				</span></i>
			:—of troops, <i>fresh</i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				18.10.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen.,
				<i>untouched by</i> . ., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῶν κατηπειλημένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					1147
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόρους ἀκραιφνεῖς μυρρίνης</span>
			<i>free from</i> . ., <i><span class="en">
				Lysipp.
				9
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
